data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","output_index":5,"item_id":"msg_tmp_stteyq7npvl","content_index":0,"text":"## Short answer\n\nOpenRouter's Responses API is an OpenAI-compatible implementation of OpenAI's `/responses` endpoint, hosted at:\n\n```\nhttps://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses\n```\n\nIt's designed as a **drop-in replacement** for OpenAI's Responses API, but it routes to **any model on OpenRouter** (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, open-source, etc.) through one unified interface, using your OpenRouter API key. OpenRouter's docs describe it as following the \"OpenResponses API format.\"\n\n## What it gives you\n\n- **Reasoning support** — configurable effort levels, reasoning summaries, encrypted reasoning chains\n- **Tool calling** — function tools, parallel tool calls, plus OpenRouter's own *server tools* (e.g. `openrouter:web_search`) that run inside the request rather than round-tripping to your code\n- **Web search** — real-time retrieval with citation annotations\n- **Text + image outputs** via `modalities`\n- **Streaming** — SSE events in the OpenAI shape (`response.created`, `response.output_item.added`, `response.content_part.delta`, `response.done`, `[DONE]`)\n\nBasic call:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"model\": \"openai/o4-mini\", \"input\": \"Hello, world!\"}'\n```\n\nYou send `input` (a string or an item array) instead of `messages`, and get back a `response` object with an `output` array of typed items:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"resp_1234567890\",\n  \"object\": \"response\",\n  \"output\": [{\n    \"type\": \"message\",\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": [{ \"type\": \"output_text\", \"text\": \"...\", \"annotations\": [] }]\n  }],\n  \"usage\": { \"input_tokens\": 12, \"output_tokens\": 45, \"total_tokens\": 57 },\n  \"status\": \"completed\"\n}\n```\n\n## The big caveat: it's stateless\n\nThis is the main difference from OpenAI's version. Each request is **independent — no server-side state is persisted**. Consequences:\n\n- `store: true` and `previous_response_id` are **rejected with a 400**\n- There's no server-side conversation object to reference; you must **resend the full conversation history in `input`** on every turn\n- You can't retrieve a stored response later (`GET /responses/{id}`)\n\nSo the \"stateful\" half of OpenAI's Responses API story doesn't carry over — you get the new request/response *shape* and tool/reasoning features, not the persistence layer.\n\n## OpenRouter-specific extras\n\nBeyond OpenAI parity, the endpoint accepts OpenRouter-flavored parameters:\n\n| Parameter | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `session_id` | Sticky routing key so a conversation lands on the same provider → better prompt-cache hit rates; also groups requests in observability |\n| `cache_control` / `prompt_cache_key` | Explicit prompt caching breakpoints, converted to each provider's native format; `ttl` of `30m` or `12h` |\n| `max_tool_calls` / `stop_server_tools_when` | Caps the server-tool agent loop (default/max 30 steps) or halts it on conditions like `step_count_is` or `max_cost` |\n| `provider` | Routing preferences among upstreams (fallbacks, ordering, etc.) |\n| `plugins` | e.g. auto-router, alignment/moderation plugins |\n| `service_tier` | `auto`, `default`, `flex`, `priority` (`fast` alias), `ultrafast`, `scale` |\n| `openrouter_metadata` | Opt-in header to surface which provider actually served the request |\n\nErrors come back in a structured envelope: `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\"}, \"metadata\": null}`.\n\n## Migrating from OpenAI\n\nThree things change: swap the base URL to `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`, use an OpenRouter key, and **prefix model IDs with the provider** (`openai/o4-mini`, `anthropic/claude-...`). Then strip any stateful usage (`store`, `previous_response_id`) and manage history client-side.\n\nDocs: `openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/overview` (guides) and `openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/responses/create-a-response` (full parameter reference). There's also a TypeScript client SDK wrapper if you'd rather not hand-roll requests.\n\nOne note: since this endpoint is newer than `/chat/completions`, feature parity across providers is uneven — capabilities like reasoning summaries or `verbosity` are model-dependent, so it's worth testing against the specific models you plan to use.","logprobs":[],"sequence_number":565}

data: {"type":"response.content_part.done","output_index":5,"item_id":"msg_tmp_stteyq7npvl","content_index":0,"part":{"type":"output_text","text":"## Short answer\n\nOpenRouter's Responses API is an OpenAI-compatible implementation of OpenAI's `/responses` endpoint, hosted at:\n\n```\nhttps://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses\n```\n\nIt's designed as a **drop-in replacement** for OpenAI's Responses API, but it routes to **any model on OpenRouter** (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, open-source, etc.) through one unified interface, using your OpenRouter API key. OpenRouter's docs describe it as following the \"OpenResponses API format.\"\n\n## What it gives you\n\n- **Reasoning support** — configurable effort levels, reasoning summaries, encrypted reasoning chains\n- **Tool calling** — function tools, parallel tool calls, plus OpenRouter's own *server tools* (e.g. `openrouter:web_search`) that run inside the request rather than round-tripping to your code\n- **Web search** — real-time retrieval with citation annotations\n- **Text + image outputs** via `modalities`\n- **Streaming** — SSE events in the OpenAI shape (`response.created`, `response.output_item.added`, `response.content_part.delta`, `response.done`, `[DONE]`)\n\nBasic call:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"model\": \"openai/o4-mini\", \"input\": \"Hello, world!\"}'\n```\n\nYou send `input` (a string or an item array) instead of `messages`, and get back a `response` object with an `output` array of typed items:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"resp_1234567890\",\n  \"object\": \"response\",\n  \"output\": [{\n    \"type\": \"message\",\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": [{ \"type\": \"output_text\", \"text\": \"...\", \"annotations\": [] }]\n  }],\n  \"usage\": { \"input_tokens\": 12, \"output_tokens\": 45, \"total_tokens\": 57 },\n  \"status\": \"completed\"\n}\n```\n\n## The big caveat: it's stateless\n\nThis is the main difference from OpenAI's version. Each request is **independent — no server-side state is persisted**. Consequences:\n\n- `store: true` and `previous_response_id` are **rejected with a 400**\n- There's no server-side conversation object to reference; you must **resend the full conversation history in `input`** on every turn\n- You can't retrieve a stored response later (`GET /responses/{id}`)\n\nSo the \"stateful\" half of OpenAI's Responses API story doesn't carry over — you get the new request/response *shape* and tool/reasoning features, not the persistence layer.\n\n## OpenRouter-specific extras\n\nBeyond OpenAI parity, the endpoint accepts OpenRouter-flavored parameters:\n\n| Parameter | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `session_id` | Sticky routing key so a conversation lands on the same provider → better prompt-cache hit rates; also groups requests in observability |\n| `cache_control` / `prompt_cache_key` | Explicit prompt caching breakpoints, converted to each provider's native format; `ttl` of `30m` or `12h` |\n| `max_tool_calls` / `stop_server_tools_when` | Caps the server-tool agent loop (default/max 30 steps) or halts it on conditions like `step_count_is` or `max_cost` |\n| `provider` | Routing preferences among upstreams (fallbacks, ordering, etc.) |\n| `plugins` | e.g. auto-router, alignment/moderation plugins |\n| `service_tier` | `auto`, `default`, `flex`, `priority` (`fast` alias), `ultrafast`, `scale` |\n| `openrouter_metadata` | Opt-in header to surface which provider actually served the request |\n\nErrors come back in a structured envelope: `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\"}, \"metadata\": null}`.\n\n## Migrating from OpenAI\n\nThree things change: swap the base URL to `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`, use an OpenRouter key, and **prefix model IDs with the provider** (`openai/o4-mini`, `anthropic/claude-...`). Then strip any stateful usage (`store`, `previous_response_id`) and manage history client-side.\n\nDocs: `openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/overview` (guides) and `openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/responses/create-a-response` (full parameter reference). There's also a TypeScript client SDK wrapper if you'd rather not hand-roll requests.\n\nOne note: since this endpoint is newer than `/chat/completions`, feature parity across providers is uneven — capabilities like reasoning summaries or `verbosity` are model-dependent, so it's worth testing against the specific models you plan to use.","annotations":[{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/overview","title":"OpenRouter Responses API - OpenAI-Compatible Documentation","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"OpenRouter’s Responses API provides OpenAI-compatible access to multiple AI models through a unified interface, designed to be a drop-in replacement for OpenAI’s Responses API. This stateless API offers enhanced capabilities including reasoning, tool calling, and web search integration, with each request being independent and no server-side state persisted.\n\nBase URL\n\n```\nhttps://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses\n\n```\n\nAuthentication\n\nAll requests require authentication using your OpenRouter API key:\n\n```\nconst response = await fetch('https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    model: 'openai/o4-mini',\n    input: 'Hello, world!',\n  }),\n});\n\n```\n\n```\nimport requests\n\nresponse = requests.post(\n    'https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses',\n    headers={\n        'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    },\n    json={\n        'model': 'openai/o4-mini',\n        'input': 'Hello, world!',\n    }\n)\n\n```\n\n```\ncurl -X POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"model\": \"openai/o4-mini\",\n    \"input\": \"Hello, world!\"\n  }'\n\n```\n\nBasic Usage\n\nLearn the fundamentals of making requests with simple text input and handling responses.\n\nReasoning\n\nAccess advanced reasoning capabilities with configurable effort levels and encrypted reasoning chains.\n\nTool Calling\n\nIntegrate function calling with support for parallel execution and complex tool interactions.\n\nWeb Search\n\nEnable web search capabilities with real-time information retrieval and citation annotations.\n\nError Handling\n\nThe API returns structured error responses:\n\n```\n{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"code\": \"invalid_prompt\",\n    \"message\": \"Missing required parameter: 'model'.\"\n  },\n  \"metadata\": null\n}\n\n```\n\nFor comprehensive error handling guidance, see Error Handling."},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/responses/create-a-response","title":"Create a response - OpenRouter | Documentation","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"# Create a response\n\nCreates a streaming or non-streaming response using OpenResponses API format\n\n```\ncurl --request POST \\\n  --url https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' \\\n  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  --data '\n{\n  \"input\": \"Tell me a joke\",\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o\"\n}\n'\n\n...\n\n#### Authorizations\n\nAPI key as bearer token in Authorization header\n\nOpt-in to surface routing metadata on the response under `openrouter_metadata`. Defaults to `disabled`. The legacy header `X-OpenRouter-Experimental-Metadata` is also accepted for backward compatibility. Opt-in level for surfacing routing metadata on the response under `openrouter_metadata`.\n\n`disabled`, `enabled` \n\n`\"enabled\"`\n\n#### Body\n\nRequest schema for Responses endpoint\n\ncache_control\n\n...\n\nInput for a response request - can be a string or array of items\n\nExample:\n\n`[ { \"content\": \"What is the weather today?\", \"role\": \"user\" }]`\n\nMaximum number of server-tool (e.g. `openrouter:web_search`) agent steps the model may take during a request. Defaults to 30, which is also the maximum. Ignored when `stop_server_tools_when` is set.\n\nExample:\n\n`30`\n\n...\n\nmodalities\n\nOutput modalities for the response. Supported values are \"text\" and \"image\".\n\n...\n\nmodel\n\nparallel_tool_calls\n\n...\n\npresence_penalty\n\nNot supported on this proxy. Each response request is independent: no responses are stored, so a previous response cannot be referenced. Requests with a non-null value are rejected with a 400 error. Send the full conversation history in `input` instead.\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"id\": \"prompt-abc123\", \"variables\": { \"name\": \"John\" }}`\n\n...\n\nreasoning\n\nConfiguration for reasoning mode in the response\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"effort\": \"medium\", \"summary\": \"auto\", \"enabled\": true}`\n\n...\n\n#### Response\n\n200\n\napplication/json\n\nSuccessful response\n\nComplete non-streaming response from the Responses API\n\ncompleted_at\n\ninteger | null required"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/basic-usage","title":"Responses API Basic Usage - Simple Text Requests","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"# Basic Usage\n\nGetting started with the Responses API\n\nThe Responses API supports both simple string input and structured message arrays, making it easy to get started with basic text generation.\n\nSimple String Input\n\nThe simplest way to use the API is with a string input:\n\n```\nconst response = await fetch('https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    model: 'openai/o4-mini',\n    input: 'What is the meaning of life?',\n    max_output_tokens: 9000,\n  }),\n});\n\nconst result = await response.json();\nconsole.log(result);\n\n```\n\n```\nimport requests\n\nresponse = requests.post(\n    'https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses',\n    headers={\n        'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    },\n    json={\n        'model': 'openai/o4-mini',\n        'input': 'What is the meaning of life?',\n        'max_output_tokens': 9000,\n    }\n)\n\nresult = response.json()\nprint(result)\n\n```\n\n```\ncurl -X POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"model\": \"openai/o4-mini\",\n    \"input\": \"What is the meaning of life?\",\n    \"max_output_tokens\": 9000\n  }'\n\n```\n\nStructured Message Input\n\nFor more complex conversations, use the message array format:\n\n```\nconst response = await fetch('https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    model: 'openai/o4-mini',\n    input: [\n      {\n        type: 'message',\n        role: 'user',\n        content: [\n          {\n            type: 'input_text',\n            text: 'Tell me a joke about programming',\n          },\n        ],\n      },\n    ],\n    max_output_tokens: 9000,\n  }),\n});\n\nconst result = await response.json();\n\n```\n\n...\n\nResponse Format\n\nThe API returns a structured response with the generated content:\n\n```\n{\n  \"id\": \"resp_1234567890\",\n  \"object\": \"response\",\n  \"created_at\": 1234567890,\n  \"model\": \"openai/o4-mini\",\n  \"output\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"message\",\n      \"id\": \"msg_abc123\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"output_text\",\n          \"text\": \"The meaning of life is a philosophical question that has been pondered for centuries...\",\n          \"annotations\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"input_tokens\": 12,\n    \"output_tokens\": 45,\n    \"total_tokens\": 57\n  },\n  \"status\": \"completed\"\n}\n\n```\n\nStreaming Responses\n\nEnable streaming for real-time response generation:\n\n```\nconst response = await fetch('https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    model: 'openai/o4-mini',\n    input: 'Write a short story about AI',\n    stream: true,\n    max_output_tokens: 9000,\n  }),\n});\n\nconst reader = response.body?.getReader();\nconst decoder = new TextDecoder();\n\nwhile (true) {\n  const { done, value } = await reader.read();\n  if (done) break;\n\n  const chunk = decoder.decode(value);\n  const lines = chunk.split('\\n');\n\n  for (const line of lines) {\n    if (line.startsWith('data: ')) {\n      const data = line.slice(6);\n      if (data === '[DONE]') return;\n\n      try {\n        const parsed = JSON.parse(data);\n        console.log(parsed);\n      } catch (e) {\n        // Skip invalid JSON\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n...\n\nExample Streaming Output\n\nThe streaming response returns Server-Sent Events (SSE) chunks:\n\n```\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.created\",\"response\":{\"id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"object\":\"response\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.output_item.added\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"item\":{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"msg_abc123\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"content\":[]}}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.added\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"part\":{\"type\":\"output_text\",\"text\":\"\"}}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.delta\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"delta\":\"Once\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.delta\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"delta\":\" upon\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.delta\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"delta\":\" a\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.delta\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"delta\":\" time\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.output_item.done\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"item\":{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"msg_abc123\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"output_text\",\"text\":\"Once upon a time, in a world where artificial intelligence had become as common as smartphones...\"}]}}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.done\",\"response\":{\"id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"object\":\"response\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":12,\"output_tokens\":45,\"total_tokens\":57}}}\n\ndata: [DONE]\n\n```\n\nCommon Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `model` | string | Required. Model to use (e.g., `openai/o4-mini`) |\n| `input` | string or array | Required. Text or message array |\n| `stream` | boolean | Enable streaming responses (default: false) |\n| `max_output_tokens` | integer | Maximum tokens to generate |\n| `temperature` | number | Sampling temperature (0-2) |\n| `top_p` | number | Nucleus sampling parameter (0-1) |\n\nError Handling\n\n...\n\nMultiple Turn Conversations\n\nSince the Responses API is stateless, you must include the full conversation history in each request to maintain context. Stateful parameters like `store: true` and `previous_response_id` are not supported and are rejected with a `400` error:\n\n```"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/responses/create-a-response","title":"Create a response - OpenRouter | Documentation","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"```\ncurl --request POST \\\n  --url https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' \\\n  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  --data '\n{\n  \"input\": \"Tell me a joke\",\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o
\"\n}\n'\n```\n\n...\n\n# Create a response\n\nCreates a streaming or non-streaming response using OpenResponses API format\n\n```\ncurl --request POST \\\n  --url https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' \\\n  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  --data '\n{\n  \"input\": \"Tell me a joke\",\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o\"\n}\n'\n```\n\n```\nimport requests\n\n...\n\npayload = {\n    \"input\": \"Tell me a joke\",\n    \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o\"\n}\nheaders = {\n    \"Authorization\": \"Bearer <token>\",\n    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n}\n\nresponse = requests.post(url, json=payload, headers=headers)\n\n...\n\n\"incomplete_details\": null,\n  \"instructions\": null,\n  \"max_output_tokens\": null,\n  \"metadata\": null,\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o\",\n  \"object\": \"response\",\n  \"output\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": [\n\n...\n\n\"annotations\": [],\n          \"text\":\n\n...\n\n}\n      ],\n\n...\n\n\"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n\n...\n\n}\n\n...\n\n\"presence_penalty\": null,\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"temperature\": null,\n\n...\n\n#### Authorizations\n\nAPI key as bearer token in Authorization header\n\nOpt-in to surface routing metadata on the response under `openrouter_metadata`. Defaults to `disabled`. The legacy header `X-OpenRouter-Experimental-Metadata` is also accepted for backward compatibility. Opt-in level for surfacing routing metadata on the response under `openrouter_metadata`.\n\n`disabled`, `enabled` \n\n`\"enabled\"`\n\n#### Body\n\nRequest schema for Responses endpoint\n\ncache_control\n\nEnable automatic prompt caching. When set at the top level, the system automatically applies cache breakpoints to the last cacheable block in the request. When set on an individual content block, it marks an explicit cache breakpoint; block-level markers also work on OpenAI models that support explicit prompt caching — OpenRouter converts them to the provider's native format.\n\n`{ \"type\": \"ephemeral\" }`\n\nDebug options for inspecting request transformations (streaming only)\n\n`{ \"echo_upstream_body\": true }`\n\nOpt-in versioned router-level deferred-tool protocol. Replay assistant reasoning unchanged on continuation; keep the catalog unchanged.\n\n`{ \"profile\": \"portable\", \"protocol\": \"v1\", \"search\": { \"max_results\": 5, \"type\": \"bm25\" }, \"validation\": \"runtime\"}`\n\nfrequency_penalty\n\nProvider-specific image configuration options. Keys and values vary by model/provider. See https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/multimodal/image-generation for more details.\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"aspect_ratio\": \"16:9\", \"quality\": \"high\" }`\n\nAvailable options: \n\n`file_search_call.results`, \n\n`message.input_image.image_url`, \n\n`computer_call_output.output.image_url`, \n\n`reasoning.encrypted_content`, \n\n`code_interpreter_call.outputs` \n\nInput for a response request - can be a string or array of items\n\nExample:\n\n`[ { \"content\": \"What is the weather today?\", \"role\": \"user\" }]`\n\nMaximum number of server-tool (e.g. `openrouter:web_search`) agent steps the model may take during a request. Defaults to 30, which is also the maximum. Ignored when `stop_server_tools_when` is set.\n\nExample:\n\n`30`\n\nmetadata\n\nMetadata key-value pairs for the request. Keys must be ≤64 characters and cannot contain brackets. Values must be ≤512 characters. Maximum 16 pairs allowed.\n\nShow child attributes\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"session_id\": \"abc-def-ghi\", \"user_id\": \"123\"}`\n\nmodalities\n\nOutput modalities for the response. Supported values are \"text\" and \"image\".\n\n`text`, `image` \n\nExample:\n\n`[\"text\", \"image\"]`\n\nmodel\n\nparallel_tool_calls\n\nPlugins you want to enable for this request, including their settings.\n\n- Option 1\n- Option 2\n- Option 3\n- Option 4\n- Option 5\n- Option 6\n- Option 7\n- Option 8\n- Option 9\n- Option 10\n- Option 11\n- Option 12\n- Option 13\n- Option 14\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"allowed_models\": [\"anthropic/*\", \"openai/*\"], \"cost_tier\": \"low\", \"enabled\": true, \"excluded_models\": [\"openai/gpt-4o\"], \"id\": \"auto-router\", \"pin_model\": false}`\n\npresence_penalty\n\nNot supported on this proxy. Each response request is independent: no responses are stored, so a previous response cannot be referenced. Requests with a non-null value are rejected with a 400 error. Send the full conversation history in `input` instead.\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"id\": \"prompt-abc123\", \"variables\": { \"name\": \"John\" }}`\n\nprompt_cache_key\n\nRequest-level prompt-cache controls. `mode: \"explicit\"` disables OpenAI-managed breakpoints so only blocks marked with `prompt_cache_breakpoint` are cached. `ttl` sets the minimum cache lifetime for every breakpoint the request writes: \"30m\" (default) or \"12h\" (billed at the higher 12h cache-write rate). Only supported by OpenAI GPT-5.6 and newer.\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"mode\": \"explicit\", \"ttl\": \"30m\" }`\n\nWhen multiple model providers are available, optionally indicate your routing preference.\n\nShow child attributes\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"allow_fallbacks\": true }`\n\nreasoning\n\nConfiguration for reasoning mode in the response\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"effort\": \"medium\", \"summary\": \"auto\", \"enabled\": true}`\n\nroute\n\n...\n\nsafety_identifier\n\n...\n\nenum | null default: auto\n\nThe service tier to use for processing this request. `fast` is accepted as an alias for `priority`. `ultrafast` prefers ultrafast endpoints and falls back to `priority`, then default endpoints.\n\n`auto`, `default`, `fast`, `flex`, `priority`, `scale`, `ultrafast`, `null` \n\nsession_id\n\nA unique identifier for grouping related requests (e.g., a conversation or agent workflow). When provided, OpenRouter uses it as the sticky routing key, routing all requests in the session to the same provider to maximize prompt cache hits. Also used for observability grouping. If provided in both the request body and the x-session-id header, the body value takes precedence. Maximum of 256 characters.\n\nMaximum string length: `256`\n\nstring string[]\n\nStop sequences (up to 4)\n\nExample:\n\n`[\"\\n\"]`\n\nstop_server_tools_when\n\nStop conditions for the server-tool agent loop. Any condition firing halts the loop (OR logic). When set, this overrides `max_tool_calls`. When a condition fires while the model is still emitting tool calls, the pending tool calls are executed and one final turn is made with tool calls disabled so the response ends with a natural-language answer instead of an unfinished tool call.\n\nMinimum array length: `1`\n\nA single condition that, when met, halts the server-tool agent loop.\n\n- Option 1\n- Option 2\n- Option 3\n- Option 4\n- Option 5\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"step_count\": 5, \"type\": \"step_count_is\" }`\n\nExample:\n\n`[ { \"step_count\": 5, \"type\": \"step_count_is\" }, { \"max_cost_in_dollars\": 0.5, \"type\": \"max_cost\" }]`\n\nboolean default: false\n\nboolean default: false\n\nText output configuration including format and verbosity\n\nShow child attributes\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"format\": { \"type\": \"text\" }, \"verbosity\": \"medium\"}`\n\n...\n\n`auto` \n\nExample:\n\n`\"auto\"`\n\nFunction tool definition\n\n...\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"description\": \"Get the current weather in a location\", \"name\": \"get_weather\", \"parameters\": { \"properties\": { \"location\": { \"description\": \"The city and state\", \"type\": \"string\" }, \"unit\": { \"enum\": [\"celsius\", \"fahrenheit\"], \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"required\": [\"location\"], \"type\": \"object\" }, \"type\": \"function\"}`\n\ntop_logprobs\n\n...\n\n#### Response\n\n200\n\napplication/json\n\nSuccessful response\n\nComplete non-streaming response from the Responses API\n\ncompleted_at\n\ninteger | null required\n\ncreated_at\n\nError of a failed response; `metadata` carries OpenRouter-specific details.\n\n`{ \"code\": \"server_error\", \"message\": \"Alignment plugin: the reply could not be evaluated: evaluator_error\", \"metadata\": { \"alignment\": { \"calls\": [ { \"call\": 1, \"outcome\": \"unavailable\", \"reason\": \"evaluator_error\" } ] } }}`\n\nfrequency_penalty\n\nnumber | null required\n\nincomplete_details\n\nobject | null required"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/client-sdks/typescript/sdks/responses/README","title":"Responses - OpenRouter | Documentation","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"| --- | --- |\n| `request` | operations.CreateResponsesRequest | ✔️ | The request object to use for the request. |\n| ` ... | Used to set various options for making HTTP requests. |\n| ` ... extra headers for examples. All `Request` options, except"}],"logprobs":[]},"sequence_number":566}

data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","output_index":5,"item":{"id":"msg_tmp_stteyq7npvl","type":"message","status":"completed","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"## Short answer\n\nOpenRouter's Responses API is an OpenAI-compatible implementation of OpenAI's `/responses` endpoint, hosted at:\n\n```\nhttps://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses\n```\n\nIt's designed as a **drop-in replacement** for OpenAI's Responses API, but it routes to **any model on OpenRouter** (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, open-source, etc.) through one unified interface, using your OpenRouter API key. OpenRouter's docs describe it as following the \"OpenResponses API format.\"\n\n## What it gives you\n\n- **Reasoning support** — configurable effort levels, reasoning summaries, encrypted reasoning chains\n- **Tool calling** — function tools, parallel tool calls, plus OpenRouter's own *server tools* (e.g. `openrouter:web_search`) that run inside the request rather than round-tripping to your code\n- **Web search** — real-time retrieval with citation annotations\n- **Text + image outputs** via `modalities`\n- **Streaming** — SSE events in the OpenAI shape (`response.created`, `response.output_item.added`, `response.content_part.delta`, `response.done`, `[DONE]`)\n\nBasic call:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"model\": \"openai/o4-mini\", \"input\": \"Hello, world!\"}'\n```\n\nYou send `input` (a string or an item array) instead of `messages`, and get back a `response` object with an `output` array of typed items:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"resp_1234567890\",\n  \"object\": \"response\",\n  \"output\": [{\n    \"type\": \"message\",\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": [{ \"type\": \"output_text\", \"text\": \"...\", \"annotations\": [] }]\n  }],\n  \"usage\": { \"input_tokens\": 12, \"output_tokens\": 45, \"total_tokens\": 57 },\n  \"status\": \"completed\"\n}\n```\n\n## The big caveat: it's stateless\n\nThis is the main difference from OpenAI's version. Each request is **independent — no server-side state is persisted**. Consequences:\n\n- `store: true` and `previous_response_id` are **rejected with a 400**\n- There's no server-side conversation object to reference; you must **resend the full conversation history in `input`** on every turn\n- You can't retrieve a stored response later (`GET /responses/{id}`)\n\nSo the \"stateful\" half of OpenAI's Responses API story doesn't carry over — you get the new request/response *shape* and tool/reasoning features, not the persistence layer.\n\n## OpenRouter-specific extras\n\nBeyond OpenAI parity, the endpoint accepts OpenRouter-flavored parameters:\n\n| Parameter | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `session_id` | Sticky routing key so a conversation lands on the same provider → better prompt-cache hit rates; also groups requests in observability |\n| `cache_control` / `prompt_cache_key` | Explicit prompt caching breakpoints, converted to each provider's native format; `ttl` of `30m` or `12h` |\n| `max_tool_calls` / `stop_server_tools_when` | Caps the server-tool agent loop (default/max 30 steps) or halts it on conditions like `step_count_is` or `max_cost` |\n| `provider` | Routing preferences among upstreams (fallbacks, ordering, etc.) |\n| `plugins` | e.g. auto-router, alignment/moderation plugins |\n| `service_tier` | `auto`, `default`, `flex`, `priority` (`fast` alias), `ultrafast`, `scale` |\n| `openrouter_metadata` | Opt-in header to surface which provider actually served the request |\n\nErrors come back in a structured envelope: `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\"}, \"metadata\": null}`.\n\n## Migrating from OpenAI\n\nThree things change: swap the base URL to `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`, use an OpenRouter key, and **prefix model IDs with the provider** (`openai/o4-mini`, `anthropic/claude-...`). Then strip any stateful usage (`store`, `previous_response_id`) and manage history client-side.\n\nDocs: `openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/overview` (guides) and `openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/responses/create-a-response` (full parameter reference). There's also a TypeScript client SDK wrapper if you'd rather not hand-roll requests.\n\nOne note: since this endpoint is newer than `/chat/completions`, feature parity across providers is uneven — capabilities like reasoning summaries or `verbosity` are model-dependent, so it's worth testing against the specific models you plan to use.","annotations":[{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/overview","title":"OpenRouter Responses API - OpenAI-Compatible Documentation","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"OpenRouter’s Responses API provides OpenAI-compatible access to multiple AI models through a unified interface, designed to be a drop-in replacement for OpenAI’s Responses API. This stateless API offers enhanced capabilities including reasoning, tool calling, and web search integration, with each request being independent and no server-side state persisted.\n\nBase URL\n\n```\nhttps://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses\n\n```\n\nAuthentication\n\nAll requests require authentication using your OpenRouter API key:\n\n```\nconst response = await fetch('https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    model: 'openai/o4-mini',\n    input: 'Hello, world!',\n  }),\n});\n\n```\n\n```\nimport requests\n\nresponse = requests.post(\n    'https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses',\n    headers={\n        'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    },\n    json={\n        'model': 'openai/o4-mini',\n        'input': 'Hello, world!',\n    }\n)\n\n```\n\n```\ncurl -X POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"model\": \"openai/o4-mini\",\n    \"input\": \"Hello, world!\"\n  }'\n\n```\n\nBasic Usage\n\nLearn the fundamentals of making requests with simple text input and handling responses.\n\nReasoning\n\nAccess advanced reasoning capabilities with configurable effort levels and encrypted reasoning chains.\n\nTool Calling\n\nIntegrate function calling with support for parallel execution and complex tool interactions.\n\nWeb Search\n\nEnable web search capabilities with real-time information retrieval and citation annotations.\n\nError Handling\n\nThe API returns structured error responses:\n\n```\n{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"code\": \"invalid_prompt\",\n    \"message\": \"Missing required parameter: 'model'.\"\n  },\n  \"metadata\": null\n}\n\n```\n\nFor comprehensive error handling guidance, see Error Handling."},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/responses/create-a-response","title":"Create a response - OpenRouter | Documentation","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"# Create a response\n\nCreates a streaming or non-streaming response using OpenResponses API format\n\n```\ncurl --request POST \\\n  --url https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' \\\n  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  --data '\n{\n  \"input\": \"Tell me a joke\",\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o\"\n}\n'\n\n...\n\n#### Authorizations\n\nAPI key as bearer token in Authorization header\n\nOpt-in to surface routing metadata on the response under `openrouter_metadata`. Defaults to `disabled`. The legacy header `X-OpenRouter-Experimental-Metadata` is also accepted for backward compatibility. Opt-in level for surfacing routing metadata on the response under `openrouter_metadata`.\n\n`disabled`, `enabled` \n\n`\"enabled\"`\n\n#### Body\n\nRequest schema for Responses endpoint\n\ncache_control\n\n...\n\nInput for a response request - can be a string or array of items\n\nExample:\n\n`[ { \"content\": \"What is the weather today?\", \"role\": \"user\" }]`\n\nMaximum number of server-tool (e.g. `openrouter:web_search`) agent steps the model may take during a request. Defaults to 30, which is also the maximum. Ignored when `stop_server_tools_when` is set.\n\nExample:\n\n`30`\n\n...\n\nmodalities\n\nOutput modalities for the response. Supported values are \"text\" and \"image\".\n\n...\n\nmodel\n\nparallel_tool_calls\n\n...\n\npresence_penalty\n\nNot supported on this proxy. Each response request is independent: no responses are stored, so a previous response cannot be referenced. Requests with a non-null value are rejected with a 400 error. Send the full conversation history in `input` instead.\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"id\": \"prompt-abc123\", \"variables\": { \"name\": \"John\" }}`\n\n...\n\nreasoning\n\nConfiguration for reasoning mode in the response\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"effort\": \"medium\", \"summary\": \"auto\", \"enabled\": true}`\n\n...\n\n#### Response\n\n200\n\napplication/json\n\nSuccessful response\n\nComplete non-streaming response from the Responses API\n\ncompleted_at\n\ninteger | null required"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/basic-usage","title":"Responses API Basic Usage - Simple Text Requests","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"# Basic Usage\n\nGetting started with the Responses API\n\nThe Responses API supports both simple string input and structured message arrays, making it easy to get started with basic text generation.\n\nSimple String Input\n\nThe simplest way to use the API is with a string input:\n\n```\nconst response = await fetch('https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    model: 'openai/o4-mini',\n    input: 'What is the meaning of life?',\n    max_output_tokens: 9000,\n  }),\n});\n\nconst result = await response.json();\nconsole.log(result);\n\n```\n\n```\nimport requests\n\nresponse = requests.post(\n    'https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses',\n    headers={\n        'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    },\n    json={\n        'model': 'openai/o4-mini',\n        'input': 'What is the meaning of life?',\n        'max_output_tokens': 9000,\n    }\n)\n\nresult = response.json()\nprint(result)\n\n```\n\n```\ncurl -X POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"model\": \"openai/o4-mini\",\n    \"input\": \"What is the meaning of life?\",\n    \"max_output_tokens\": 9000\n  }'\n\n```\n\nStructured Message Input\n\nFor more complex conversations, use the message array format:\n\n```\nconst response = await fetch('https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    model: 'openai/o4-mini',\n    input: [\n      {\n        type: 'message',\n        role: 'user',\n        content: [\n          {\n            type: 'input_text',\n            text: 'Tell me a joke about programming',\n          },\n        ],\n      },\n    ],\n    max_output_tokens: 9000,\n  }),\n});\n\nconst result = await response.json();\n\n```\n\n...\n\nResponse Format\n\nThe API returns a structured response with the generated content:\n\n```\n{\n  \"id\": \"resp_1234567890\",\n  \"object\": \"response\",\n  \"created_at\": 1234567890,\n  \"model\": \"openai/o4-mini\",\n  \"output\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"message\",\n      \"id\": \"msg_abc123\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"output_text\",\n          \"text\": \"The meaning of life is a philosophical question that has been pondered for centuries...\",\n          \"annotations\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"input_tokens\": 12,\n    \"output_tokens\": 45,\n    \"total_tokens\": 57\n  },\n  \"status\": \"completed\"\n}\n\n```\n\nStreaming Responses\n\nEnable streaming for real-time response generation:\n\n```\nconst response = await fetch('https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    model: 'openai/o4-mini',\n    input: 'Write a short story about AI',\n    stream: true,\n    max_output_tokens: 9000,\n  }),\n});\n\nconst reader = response.body?.getReader();\nconst decoder = new TextDecoder();\n\nwhile (true) {\n  const { done, value } = await reader.read();\n  if (done) break;\n\n  const chunk = decoder.decode(value);\n  const lines = chunk.split('\\n');\n\n  for (const line of lines) {\n    if (line.startsWith('data: ')) {\n      const data = line.slice(6);\n      if (data === '[DONE]') return;\n\n      try {\n        const parsed = JSON.parse(data);\n        console.log(parsed);\n      } catch (e) {\n        // Skip invalid JSON\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n...\n\nExample Streaming Output\n\nThe streaming response returns Server-Sent Events (SSE) chunks:\n\n```\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.created\",\"response\":{\"id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"object\":\"response\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.output_item.added\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"item\":{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"msg_abc123\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"content\":[]}}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.added\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"part\":{\"type\":\"output_text\",\"text\":\"\"}}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.delta\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"delta\":\"Once\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.delta\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"delta\":\" upon\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.delta\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"delta\":\" a\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.delta\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"delta\":\" time\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.output_item.done\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"item\":{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"msg_abc123\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"output_text\",\"text\":\"Once upon a time, in a world where artificial intelligence had become as common as smartphones...\"}]}}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.done\",\"response\":{\"id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"object\":\"response\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":12,\"output_tokens\":45,\"total_tokens\":57}}}\n\ndata: [DONE]\n\n```\n\nCommon Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `model` | string | Required. Model to use (e.g., `openai/o4-mini`) |\n| `input` | string or array | Required. Text or message array |\n| `stream` | boolean | Enable streaming responses (default: false) |\n| `max_output_tokens` | integer | Maximum tokens to generate |\n| `temperature` | number | Sampling temperature (0-2) |\n| `top_p` | number | Nucleus sampling parameter (0-1) |\n\nError Handling\n\n...\n\nMultiple Turn Conversations\n\nSince the Responses API is stateless, you must include the full conversation history in each request to maintain context. Stateful parameters like `store: true` and `previous_response_id` are not supported and are rejected with a `400` error:\n\n```"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/responses/create-a-response","title":"Create a response - OpenRouter | Documentation","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"```\ncurl --request POST \\\n  --url https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' \\\n  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  --data '\n{\n  \"input\": \"Te
ll me a joke\",\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o\"\n}\n'\n```\n\n...\n\n# Create a response\n\nCreates a streaming or non-streaming response using OpenResponses API format\n\n```\ncurl --request POST \\\n  --url https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' \\\n  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  --data '\n{\n  \"input\": \"Tell me a joke\",\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o\"\n}\n'\n```\n\n```\nimport requests\n\n...\n\npayload = {\n    \"input\": \"Tell me a joke\",\n    \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o\"\n}\nheaders = {\n    \"Authorization\": \"Bearer <token>\",\n    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n}\n\nresponse = requests.post(url, json=payload, headers=headers)\n\n...\n\n\"incomplete_details\": null,\n  \"instructions\": null,\n  \"max_output_tokens\": null,\n  \"metadata\": null,\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o\",\n  \"object\": \"response\",\n  \"output\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": [\n\n...\n\n\"annotations\": [],\n          \"text\":\n\n...\n\n}\n      ],\n\n...\n\n\"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n\n...\n\n}\n\n...\n\n\"presence_penalty\": null,\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"temperature\": null,\n\n...\n\n#### Authorizations\n\nAPI key as bearer token in Authorization header\n\nOpt-in to surface routing metadata on the response under `openrouter_metadata`. Defaults to `disabled`. The legacy header `X-OpenRouter-Experimental-Metadata` is also accepted for backward compatibility. Opt-in level for surfacing routing metadata on the response under `openrouter_metadata`.\n\n`disabled`, `enabled` \n\n`\"enabled\"`\n\n#### Body\n\nRequest schema for Responses endpoint\n\ncache_control\n\nEnable automatic prompt caching. When set at the top level, the system automatically applies cache breakpoints to the last cacheable block in the request. When set on an individual content block, it marks an explicit cache breakpoint; block-level markers also work on OpenAI models that support explicit prompt caching — OpenRouter converts them to the provider's native format.\n\n`{ \"type\": \"ephemeral\" }`\n\nDebug options for inspecting request transformations (streaming only)\n\n`{ \"echo_upstream_body\": true }`\n\nOpt-in versioned router-level deferred-tool protocol. Replay assistant reasoning unchanged on continuation; keep the catalog unchanged.\n\n`{ \"profile\": \"portable\", \"protocol\": \"v1\", \"search\": { \"max_results\": 5, \"type\": \"bm25\" }, \"validation\": \"runtime\"}`\n\nfrequency_penalty\n\nProvider-specific image configuration options. Keys and values vary by model/provider. See https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/multimodal/image-generation for more details.\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"aspect_ratio\": \"16:9\", \"quality\": \"high\" }`\n\nAvailable options: \n\n`file_search_call.results`, \n\n`message.input_image.image_url`, \n\n`computer_call_output.output.image_url`, \n\n`reasoning.encrypted_content`, \n\n`code_interpreter_call.outputs` \n\nInput for a response request - can be a string or array of items\n\nExample:\n\n`[ { \"content\": \"What is the weather today?\", \"role\": \"user\" }]`\n\nMaximum number of server-tool (e.g. `openrouter:web_search`) agent steps the model may take during a request. Defaults to 30, which is also the maximum. Ignored when `stop_server_tools_when` is set.\n\nExample:\n\n`30`\n\nmetadata\n\nMetadata key-value pairs for the request. Keys must be ≤64 characters and cannot contain brackets. Values must be ≤512 characters. Maximum 16 pairs allowed.\n\nShow child attributes\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"session_id\": \"abc-def-ghi\", \"user_id\": \"123\"}`\n\nmodalities\n\nOutput modalities for the response. Supported values are \"text\" and \"image\".\n\n`text`, `image` \n\nExample:\n\n`[\"text\", \"image\"]`\n\nmodel\n\nparallel_tool_calls\n\nPlugins you want to enable for this request, including their settings.\n\n- Option 1\n- Option 2\n- Option 3\n- Option 4\n- Option 5\n- Option 6\n- Option 7\n- Option 8\n- Option 9\n- Option 10\n- Option 11\n- Option 12\n- Option 13\n- Option 14\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"allowed_models\": [\"anthropic/*\", \"openai/*\"], \"cost_tier\": \"low\", \"enabled\": true, \"excluded_models\": [\"openai/gpt-4o\"], \"id\": \"auto-router\", \"pin_model\": false}`\n\npresence_penalty\n\nNot supported on this proxy. Each response request is independent: no responses are stored, so a previous response cannot be referenced. Requests with a non-null value are rejected with a 400 error. Send the full conversation history in `input` instead.\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"id\": \"prompt-abc123\", \"variables\": { \"name\": \"John\" }}`\n\nprompt_cache_key\n\nRequest-level prompt-cache controls. `mode: \"explicit\"` disables OpenAI-managed breakpoints so only blocks marked with `prompt_cache_breakpoint` are cached. `ttl` sets the minimum cache lifetime for every breakpoint the request writes: \"30m\" (default) or \"12h\" (billed at the higher 12h cache-write rate). Only supported by OpenAI GPT-5.6 and newer.\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"mode\": \"explicit\", \"ttl\": \"30m\" }`\n\nWhen multiple model providers are available, optionally indicate your routing preference.\n\nShow child attributes\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"allow_fallbacks\": true }`\n\nreasoning\n\nConfiguration for reasoning mode in the response\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"effort\": \"medium\", \"summary\": \"auto\", \"enabled\": true}`\n\nroute\n\n...\n\nsafety_identifier\n\n...\n\nenum | null default: auto\n\nThe service tier to use for processing this request. `fast` is accepted as an alias for `priority`. `ultrafast` prefers ultrafast endpoints and falls back to `priority`, then default endpoints.\n\n`auto`, `default`, `fast`, `flex`, `priority`, `scale`, `ultrafast`, `null` \n\nsession_id\n\nA unique identifier for grouping related requests (e.g., a conversation or agent workflow). When provided, OpenRouter uses it as the sticky routing key, routing all requests in the session to the same provider to maximize prompt cache hits. Also used for observability grouping. If provided in both the request body and the x-session-id header, the body value takes precedence. Maximum of 256 characters.\n\nMaximum string length: `256`\n\nstring string[]\n\nStop sequences (up to 4)\n\nExample:\n\n`[\"\\n\"]`\n\nstop_server_tools_when\n\nStop conditions for the server-tool agent loop. Any condition firing halts the loop (OR logic). When set, this overrides `max_tool_calls`. When a condition fires while the model is still emitting tool calls, the pending tool calls are executed and one final turn is made with tool calls disabled so the response ends with a natural-language answer instead of an unfinished tool call.\n\nMinimum array length: `1`\n\nA single condition that, when met, halts the server-tool agent loop.\n\n- Option 1\n- Option 2\n- Option 3\n- Option 4\n- Option 5\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"step_count\": 5, \"type\": \"step_count_is\" }`\n\nExample:\n\n`[ { \"step_count\": 5, \"type\": \"step_count_is\" }, { \"max_cost_in_dollars\": 0.5, \"type\": \"max_cost\" }]`\n\nboolean default: false\n\nboolean default: false\n\nText output configuration including format and verbosity\n\nShow child attributes\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"format\": { \"type\": \"text\" }, \"verbosity\": \"medium\"}`\n\n...\n\n`auto` \n\nExample:\n\n`\"auto\"`\n\nFunction tool definition\n\n...\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"description\": \"Get the current weather in a location\", \"name\": \"get_weather\", \"parameters\": { \"properties\": { \"location\": { \"description\": \"The city and state\", \"type\": \"string\" }, \"unit\": { \"enum\": [\"celsius\", \"fahrenheit\"], \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"required\": [\"location\"], \"type\": \"object\" }, \"type\": \"function\"}`\n\ntop_logprobs\n\n...\n\n#### Response\n\n200\n\napplication/json\n\nSuccessful response\n\nComplete non-streaming response from the Responses API\n\ncompleted_at\n\ninteger | null required\n\ncreated_at\n\nError of a failed response; `metadata` carries OpenRouter-specific details.\n\n`{ \"code\": \"server_error\", \"message\": \"Alignment plugin: the reply could not be evaluated: evaluator_error\", \"metadata\": { \"alignment\": { \"calls\": [ { \"call\": 1, \"outcome\": \"unavailable\", \"reason\": \"evaluator_error\" } ] } }}`\n\nfrequency_penalty\n\nnumber | null required\n\nincomplete_details\n\nobject | null required"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/client-sdks/typescript/sdks/responses/README","title":"Responses - OpenRouter | Documentation","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"| --- | --- |\n| `request` | operations.CreateResponsesRequest | ✔️ | The request object to use for the request. |\n| ` ... | Used to set various options for making HTTP requests. |\n| ` ... extra headers for examples. All `Request` options, except"}],"logprobs":[]}]},"sequence_number":567}

data: {"type":"response.completed","response":{"id":"gen-1793231291-6r9gXvQLtms1EocxNdOa","object":"response","created_at":1793231292,"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017","status":"completed","completed_at":1793231305,"output":[{"id":"rs_tmp_2k5dfdvgtqh","type":"reasoning","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"reasoning_text","text":"The user asks about OpenRouter's Responses API. Let me search for it since this is recent info.\n\nLet me do a search."}],"summary":[]},{"id":"msg_tmp_5bpxfwrfrwi","type":"message","role":"assistant","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"I'll look this up to give you accurate, current details.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}]},{"type":"openrouter:web_search","id":"st_tmp_064ro5ptbocl","status":"completed","action":{"type":"search","query":"OpenRouter Responses API","sources":[{"type":"url","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/overview"},{"type":"url","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/responses/create-a-response"},{"type":"url","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/basic-usage"}]}},{"type":"openrouter:web_search","id":"st_tmp_p0l0aikyh6","status":"completed","action":{"type":"search","query":"OpenRouter Responses API OpenAI-compatible /responses endpoint documentation 2026","sources":[{"type":"url","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/overview"},{"type":"url","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/responses/create-a-response"},{"type":"url","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/client-sdks/typescript/sdks/responses/README"}]}},{"id":"rs_tmp_ktle5l1eac","type":"reasoning","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"reasoning_text","text":"I have good info. Let me write an answer.\n\nKey points:\n- OpenAI-compatible endpoint at https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses\n- Drop-in replacement for OpenAI's Responses API\n- Stateless: each request independent, no server-side state, so store: true and previous_response_id rejected with 400\n- Supports reasoning (effort levels, encrypted reasoning chains), tool calling (parallel, function tools), web search (server tools like openrouter:web_search with annotations/citations)\n- Input can be string or array of items; supports text and image modalities\n- Streaming via SSE with events like response.created, response.output_item.added, response.content_part.delta, response.done\n- Errors structured: {\"error\": {\"code\", \"message\"}, \"metadata\": null}\n- Extra OpenRouter-specific features: openrouter_metadata header opt-in, session_id for sticky routing, cache_control / prompt_cache_key, max_tool_calls / stop_server_tools_when for server-tool agent loop, provider routing preferences, service_tier, plugins\n- Note: differs from Chat Completions — use `input`/`instructions`/`max_output_tokens` instead of messages/max_tokens. No stateful features.\n- How to migrate: point base URL to OpenRouter, prefix model names with provider (openai/o4-mini, anthropic/claude-...), use OpenRouter API key.\n\nAlso mention it's relatively new (2025 rollout). Maybe mention two flavors: /responses and the older /chat/completions endpoint.\n\nShould I mention \"OpenResponses API format\"? Yes, one doc says \"using OpenResponses API format\".\n\nLet me write a concise but useful answer with a code sample, key differences table, and gotchas.\n\nI should be careful about claims I'm not sure about. E.g., whether web search tool is `openrouter:web_search` — the doc excerpt mentions `openrouter:web_search` as an example server tool. Good.\n\nLet me structure:\n1. What it is (one paragraph)\n2. Endpoint & basic usage\n3. Capabilities\n4. Key differences from OpenAI's version (stateless)\n5. OpenRouter-specific extras\n6. Migration notes\n\nKeep it reasonably tight."}],"summary":[]},{"id":"msg_tmp_stteyq7npvl","type":"message","role":"assistant","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"## Short answer\n\nOpenRouter's Responses API is an OpenAI-compatible implementation of OpenAI's `/responses` endpoint, hosted at:\n\n```\nhttps://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses\n```\n\nIt's designed as a **drop-in replacement** for OpenAI's Responses API, but it routes to **any model on OpenRouter** (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, open-source, etc.) through one unified interface, using your OpenRouter API key. OpenRouter's docs describe it as following the \"OpenResponses API format.\"\n\n## What it gives you\n\n- **Reasoning support** — configurable effort levels, reasoning summaries, encrypted reasoning chains\n- **Tool calling** — function tools, parallel tool calls, plus OpenRouter's own *server tools* (e.g. `openrouter:web_search`) that run inside the request rather than round-tripping to your code\n- **Web search** — real-time retrieval with citation annotations\n- **Text + image outputs** via `modalities`\n- **Streaming** — SSE events in the OpenAI shape (`response.created`, `response.output_item.added`, `response.content_part.delta`, `response.done`, `[DONE]`)\n\nBasic call:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"model\": \"openai/o4-mini\", \"input\": \"Hello, world!\"}'\n```\n\nYou send `input` (a string or an item array) instead of `messages`, and get back a `response` object with an `output` array of typed items:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"resp_1234567890\",\n  \"object\": \"response\",\n  \"output\": [{\n    \"type\": \"message\",\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": [{ \"type\": \"output_text\", \"text\": \"...\", \"annotations\": [] }]\n  }],\n  \"usage\": { \"input_tokens\": 12, \"output_tokens\": 45, \"total_tokens\": 57 },\n  \"status\": \"completed\"\n}\n```\n\n## The big caveat: it's stateless\n\nThis is the main difference from OpenAI's version. Each request is **independent — no server-side state is persisted**. Consequences:\n\n- `store: true` and `previous_response_id` are **rejected with a 400**\n- There's no server-side conversation object to reference; you must **resend the full conversation history in `input`** on every turn\n- You can't retrieve a stored response later (`GET /responses/{id}`)\n\nSo the \"stateful\" half of OpenAI's Responses API story doesn't carry over — you get the new request/response *shape* and tool/reasoning features, not the persistence layer.\n\n## OpenRouter-specific extras\n\nBeyond OpenAI parity, the endpoint accepts OpenRouter-flavored parameters:\n\n| Parameter | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `session_id` | Sticky routing key so a conversation lands on the same provider → better prompt-cache hit rates; also groups requests in observability |\n| `cache_control` / `prompt_cache_key` | Explicit prompt caching breakpoints, converted to each provider's native format; `ttl` of `30m` or `12h` |\n| `max_tool_calls` / `stop_server_tools_when` | Caps the server-tool agent loop (default/max 30 steps) or halts it on conditions like `step_count_is` or `max_cost` |\n| `provider` | Routing preferences among upstreams (fallbacks, ordering, etc.) |\n| `plugins` | e.g. auto-router, alignment/moderation plugins |\n| `service_tier` | `auto`, `default`, `flex`, `priority` (`fast` alias), `ultrafast`, `scale` |\n| `openrouter_metadata` | Opt-in header to surface which provider actually served the request |\n\nErrors come back in a structured envelope: `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\"}, \"metadata\": null}`.\n\n## Migrating from OpenAI\n\nThree things change: swap the base URL to `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`, use an OpenRouter key, and **prefix model IDs with the provider** (`openai/o4-mini`, `anthropic/claude-...`). Then strip any stateful usage (`store`, `previous_response_id`) and manage history client-side.\n\nDocs: `openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/overview` (guides) and `openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/responses/create-a-response` (full parameter reference). There's also a TypeScript client SDK wrapper if you'd rather not hand-roll requests.\n\nOne note: since this endpoint is newer than `/chat/completions`, feature parity across providers is uneven — capabilities like reasoning summaries or `verbosity` are model-dependent, so it's worth testing against the specific models you plan to use.","annotations":[{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/overview","title":"OpenRouter Responses API - OpenAI-Compatible Documentation","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"OpenRouter’s Responses API provides OpenAI-compatible access to multiple AI models through a unified interface, designed to be a drop-in replacement for OpenAI’s Responses API. This stateless API offers enhanced capabilities including reasoning, tool calling, and web search integration, with each request being independent and no server-side state persisted.\n\nBase URL\n\n```\nhttps://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses\n\n```\n\nAuthentication\n\nAll requests require authentication using your OpenRouter API key:\n\n```\nconst response = await fetch('https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    model: 'openai/o4-mini',\n    input: 'Hello, world!',\n  }),\n});\n\n```\n\n```\nimport requests\n\nresponse = requests.post(\n    'https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses',\n    headers={\n        'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    },\n    json={\n        'model': 'openai/o4-mini',\n        'input': 'Hello, world!',\n    }\n)\n\n```\n\n```\ncurl -X POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"model\": \"openai/o4-mini\",\n    \"input\": \"Hello, world!\"\n  }'\n\n```\n\nBasic Usage\n\nLearn the fundamentals of making requests with simple text input and handling responses.\n\nReasoning\n\nAccess advanced reasoning capabilities with configurable effort levels and encrypted reasoning chains.\n\nTool Calling\n\nIntegrate function calling with support for parallel execution and complex tool interactions.\n\nWeb Search\n\nEnable web search capabilities with real-time information retrieval and citation annotations.\n\nError Handling\n\nThe API returns structured error responses:\n\n```\n{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"code\": \"invalid_prompt\",\n    \"message\": \"Missing required parameter: 'model'.\"\n  },\n  \"metadata\": null\n}\n\n```\n\nFor comprehensive error handling guidance, see Error Handling."},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/responses/create-a-response","title":"Create a response - OpenRouter | Documentation","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"# Create a response\n\nCreates a streaming or non-streaming response using OpenResponses API format\n\n```\ncurl --request POST \\\n  --url https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' \\\n  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  --data '\n{\n  \"input\": \"Tell me a joke\",\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o\"\n}\n'\n\n...\n\n#### Authorizations\n\nAPI key as bearer token in Authorization header\n\nOpt-in to surface routing metadata on the response under `openrouter_metadata`. Defaults to `disabled`. The legacy header `X-OpenRouter-Experimental-Metadata` is also accepted for backward compatibility. Opt-in level for surfacing routing metadata on the response under `openrouter_metadata`.\n\n`disabled`, `enabled` \n\n`\"enabled\"`\n\n#### Body\n\nRequest schema for Responses endpoint\n\ncache_control\n\n...\n\nInput for a response request - can be a string or array of items\n\nExample:\n\n`[ { \"content\": \"What is the weather today?\", \"role\": \"user\" }]`\n\nMaximum number of server-tool (e.g. `openrouter:web_search`) agent steps the model may take during a request. Defaults to 30, which is also the maximum. Ignored when `stop_server_tools_when` is set.\n\nExample:\n\n`30`\n\n...\n\nmodalities\n\nOutput modalities for the response. Supported values are \"text\" and \"image\".\n\n...\n\nmodel\n\nparallel_tool_calls\n\n...\n\npresence_penalty\n\nNot supported on this proxy. Each response request is independent: no responses are stored, so a previous response cannot be referenced. Requests with a non-null value are rejected with a 400 error. Send the full conversation history in `input` instead.\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"id\": \"prompt-abc123\", \"variables\": { \"name\": \"John\" }}`\n\n...\n\nreasoning\n\nConfiguration for reasoning mode in the response\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"effort\": \"medium\", \"summary\": \"auto\", \"enabled\": true}`\n\n...\n\n#### Response\n\n200\n\napplication/json\n\nSuccessful response\n\nComplete non-streaming response from the Responses API\n\ncompleted_at\n\ninteger | null required"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/basic-usage","title":"Responses API Basic Usage - Simple Text Requests","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"# Basic Usage\n\nGetting started with the Responses API\n\nThe Responses API supports both simple string input and structured message arrays, making it easy to get started with basic text generation.\n\nSimple String Input\n\nThe simplest way to use the API is with a string input:\n\n```\nconst response = await fetch('https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    model: 'openai/o4-mini',\n    input: 'What is the meaning of life?',\n    max_output_tokens: 9000,\n  }),\n});\n\nconst result = await response.json();\nconsole.log(result);\n\n```\n\n```\nimport requests\n\nresponse = requests.post(\n    'https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses',\n    headers={\n        'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    },\n    json={\n        'model': 'openai/o4-mini',\n        'input': 'What is the meaning of life?',\n        'max_output_tokens': 9000,\n    }\n)\n\nresult = response.json()\nprint(result)\n\n```\n\n```\ncurl -X POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"model\": \"openai/o4-mini\",\n    \"input\": \"What is the meaning of life?\",\n    \"max_output_tokens\": 9000\n  }'\n\n```\n\nStructured Message Input\n\nFor more complex conversations, use the message array format:\n\n```\nconst response = await fetch('https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    model: 'openai/o4-mini',\n    input: [\n      {\n        type: 'message',\n        role: 'user',\n        content: [\n          {\n            type: 'input_text',\n            text: 'Tell me a joke about programming',\n          },\n        ],\n      },\n    ],\n    max_output_tokens: 9000,\n  }),\n});\n\nconst result = await response.json();\n\n```\n\n...\n\nResponse Format\n\nThe API returns a structured response with the generated content:\n\n```\n{\n  \"id\": \"resp_1234567890\",\n  \"object\": \"response\",\n  \"created_at\": 1234567890,\n  \"model\": \"openai/o4-mini\",\n  \"output\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"message\",\n      \"id\": \"msg_abc123\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"output_text\",\n          \"text\": \"The meaning of life is a philosophical question that has been pondered for centuries...\",\n          \"annotations\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"input_tokens\": 12,\n    \"output_tokens\": 45,\n    \"total_tokens\": 57\n  },\n  \"status\": \"completed\"\n}\n\n```\n\nStreaming Responses\n\nEnable streaming for real-time response generation:\n\n```\nconst response = await fetch('https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY',\n    'Content-T
ype': 'application/json',\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    model: 'openai/o4-mini',\n    input: 'Write a short story about AI',\n    stream: true,\n    max_output_tokens: 9000,\n  }),\n});\n\nconst reader = response.body?.getReader();\nconst decoder = new TextDecoder();\n\nwhile (true) {\n  const { done, value } = await reader.read();\n  if (done) break;\n\n  const chunk = decoder.decode(value);\n  const lines = chunk.split('\\n');\n\n  for (const line of lines) {\n    if (line.startsWith('data: ')) {\n      const data = line.slice(6);\n      if (data === '[DONE]') return;\n\n      try {\n        const parsed = JSON.parse(data);\n        console.log(parsed);\n      } catch (e) {\n        // Skip invalid JSON\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n...\n\nExample Streaming Output\n\nThe streaming response returns Server-Sent Events (SSE) chunks:\n\n```\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.created\",\"response\":{\"id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"object\":\"response\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.output_item.added\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"item\":{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"msg_abc123\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"content\":[]}}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.added\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"part\":{\"type\":\"output_text\",\"text\":\"\"}}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.delta\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"delta\":\"Once\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.delta\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"delta\":\" upon\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.delta\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"delta\":\" a\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.content_part.delta\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"content_index\":0,\"delta\":\" time\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.output_item.done\",\"response_id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"output_index\":0,\"item\":{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"msg_abc123\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"output_text\",\"text\":\"Once upon a time, in a world where artificial intelligence had become as common as smartphones...\"}]}}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.done\",\"response\":{\"id\":\"resp_1234567890\",\"object\":\"response\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":12,\"output_tokens\":45,\"total_tokens\":57}}}\n\ndata: [DONE]\n\n```\n\nCommon Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `model` | string | Required. Model to use (e.g., `openai/o4-mini`) |\n| `input` | string or array | Required. Text or message array |\n| `stream` | boolean | Enable streaming responses (default: false) |\n| `max_output_tokens` | integer | Maximum tokens to generate |\n| `temperature` | number | Sampling temperature (0-2) |\n| `top_p` | number | Nucleus sampling parameter (0-1) |\n\nError Handling\n\n...\n\nMultiple Turn Conversations\n\nSince the Responses API is stateless, you must include the full conversation history in each request to maintain context. Stateful parameters like `store: true` and `previous_response_id` are not supported and are rejected with a `400` error:\n\n```"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/responses/create-a-response","title":"Create a response - OpenRouter | Documentation","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"```\ncurl --request POST \\\n  --url https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' \\\n  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  --data '\n{\n  \"input\": \"Tell me a joke\",\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o\"\n}\n'\n```\n\n...\n\n# Create a response\n\nCreates a streaming or non-streaming response using OpenResponses API format\n\n```\ncurl --request POST \\\n  --url https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses \\\n  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' \\\n  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  --data '\n{\n  \"input\": \"Tell me a joke\",\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o\"\n}\n'\n```\n\n```\nimport requests\n\n...\n\npayload = {\n    \"input\": \"Tell me a joke\",\n    \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o\"\n}\nheaders = {\n    \"Authorization\": \"Bearer <token>\",\n    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n}\n\nresponse = requests.post(url, json=payload, headers=headers)\n\n...\n\n\"incomplete_details\": null,\n  \"instructions\": null,\n  \"max_output_tokens\": null,\n  \"metadata\": null,\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o\",\n  \"object\": \"response\",\n  \"output\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": [\n\n...\n\n\"annotations\": [],\n          \"text\":\n\n...\n\n}\n      ],\n\n...\n\n\"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n\n...\n\n}\n\n...\n\n\"presence_penalty\": null,\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"temperature\": null,\n\n...\n\n#### Authorizations\n\nAPI key as bearer token in Authorization header\n\nOpt-in to surface routing metadata on the response under `openrouter_metadata`. Defaults to `disabled`. The legacy header `X-OpenRouter-Experimental-Metadata` is also accepted for backward compatibility. Opt-in level for surfacing routing metadata on the response under `openrouter_metadata`.\n\n`disabled`, `enabled` \n\n`\"enabled\"`\n\n#### Body\n\nRequest schema for Responses endpoint\n\ncache_control\n\nEnable automatic prompt caching. When set at the top level, the system automatically applies cache breakpoints to the last cacheable block in the request. When set on an individual content block, it marks an explicit cache breakpoint; block-level markers also work on OpenAI models that support explicit prompt caching — OpenRouter converts them to the provider's native format.\n\n`{ \"type\": \"ephemeral\" }`\n\nDebug options for inspecting request transformations (streaming only)\n\n`{ \"echo_upstream_body\": true }`\n\nOpt-in versioned router-level deferred-tool protocol. Replay assistant reasoning unchanged on continuation; keep the catalog unchanged.\n\n`{ \"profile\": \"portable\", \"protocol\": \"v1\", \"search\": { \"max_results\": 5, \"type\": \"bm25\" }, \"validation\": \"runtime\"}`\n\nfrequency_penalty\n\nProvider-specific image configuration options. Keys and values vary by model/provider. See https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/multimodal/image-generation for more details.\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"aspect_ratio\": \"16:9\", \"quality\": \"high\" }`\n\nAvailable options: \n\n`file_search_call.results`, \n\n`message.input_image.image_url`, \n\n`computer_call_output.output.image_url`, \n\n`reasoning.encrypted_content`, \n\n`code_interpreter_call.outputs` \n\nInput for a response request - can be a string or array of items\n\nExample:\n\n`[ { \"content\": \"What is the weather today?\", \"role\": \"user\" }]`\n\nMaximum number of server-tool (e.g. `openrouter:web_search`) agent steps the model may take during a request. Defaults to 30, which is also the maximum. Ignored when `stop_server_tools_when` is set.\n\nExample:\n\n`30`\n\nmetadata\n\nMetadata key-value pairs for the request. Keys must be ≤64 characters and cannot contain brackets. Values must be ≤512 characters. Maximum 16 pairs allowed.\n\nShow child attributes\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"session_id\": \"abc-def-ghi\", \"user_id\": \"123\"}`\n\nmodalities\n\nOutput modalities for the response. Supported values are \"text\" and \"image\".\n\n`text`, `image` \n\nExample:\n\n`[\"text\", \"image\"]`\n\nmodel\n\nparallel_tool_calls\n\nPlugins you want to enable for this request, including their settings.\n\n- Option 1\n- Option 2\n- Option 3\n- Option 4\n- Option 5\n- Option 6\n- Option 7\n- Option 8\n- Option 9\n- Option 10\n- Option 11\n- Option 12\n- Option 13\n- Option 14\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"allowed_models\": [\"anthropic/*\", \"openai/*\"], \"cost_tier\": \"low\", \"enabled\": true, \"excluded_models\": [\"openai/gpt-4o\"], \"id\": \"auto-router\", \"pin_model\": false}`\n\npresence_penalty\n\nNot supported on this proxy. Each response request is independent: no responses are stored, so a previous response cannot be referenced. Requests with a non-null value are rejected with a 400 error. Send the full conversation history in `input` instead.\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"id\": \"prompt-abc123\", \"variables\": { \"name\": \"John\" }}`\n\nprompt_cache_key\n\nRequest-level prompt-cache controls. `mode: \"explicit\"` disables OpenAI-managed breakpoints so only blocks marked with `prompt_cache_breakpoint` are cached. `ttl` sets the minimum cache lifetime for every breakpoint the request writes: \"30m\" (default) or \"12h\" (billed at the higher 12h cache-write rate). Only supported by OpenAI GPT-5.6 and newer.\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"mode\": \"explicit\", \"ttl\": \"30m\" }`\n\nWhen multiple model providers are available, optionally indicate your routing preference.\n\nShow child attributes\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"allow_fallbacks\": true }`\n\nreasoning\n\nConfiguration for reasoning mode in the response\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"effort\": \"medium\", \"summary\": \"auto\", \"enabled\": true}`\n\nroute\n\n...\n\nsafety_identifier\n\n...\n\nenum | null default: auto\n\nThe service tier to use for processing this request. `fast` is accepted as an alias for `priority`. `ultrafast` prefers ultrafast endpoints and falls back to `priority`, then default endpoints.\n\n`auto`, `default`, `fast`, `flex`, `priority`, `scale`, `ultrafast`, `null` \n\nsession_id\n\nA unique identifier for grouping related requests (e.g., a conversation or agent workflow). When provided, OpenRouter uses it as the sticky routing key, routing all requests in the session to the same provider to maximize prompt cache hits. Also used for observability grouping. If provided in both the request body and the x-session-id header, the body value takes precedence. Maximum of 256 characters.\n\nMaximum string length: `256`\n\nstring string[]\n\nStop sequences (up to 4)\n\nExample:\n\n`[\"\\n\"]`\n\nstop_server_tools_when\n\nStop conditions for the server-tool agent loop. Any condition firing halts the loop (OR logic). When set, this overrides `max_tool_calls`. When a condition fires while the model is still emitting tool calls, the pending tool calls are executed and one final turn is made with tool calls disabled so the response ends with a natural-language answer instead of an unfinished tool call.\n\nMinimum array length: `1`\n\nA single condition that, when met, halts the server-tool agent loop.\n\n- Option 1\n- Option 2\n- Option 3\n- Option 4\n- Option 5\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"step_count\": 5, \"type\": \"step_count_is\" }`\n\nExample:\n\n`[ { \"step_count\": 5, \"type\": \"step_count_is\" }, { \"max_cost_in_dollars\": 0.5, \"type\": \"max_cost\" }]`\n\nboolean default: false\n\nboolean default: false\n\nText output configuration including format and verbosity\n\nShow child attributes\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"format\": { \"type\": \"text\" }, \"verbosity\": \"medium\"}`\n\n...\n\n`auto` \n\nExample:\n\n`\"auto\"`\n\nFunction tool definition\n\n...\n\nExample:\n\n`{ \"description\": \"Get the current weather in a location\", \"name\": \"get_weather\", \"parameters\": { \"properties\": { \"location\": { \"description\": \"The city and state\", \"type\": \"string\" }, \"unit\": { \"enum\": [\"celsius\", \"fahrenheit\"], \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"required\": [\"location\"], \"type\": \"object\" }, \"type\": \"function\"}`\n\ntop_logprobs\n\n...\n\n#### Response\n\n200\n\napplication/json\n\nSuccessful response\n\nComplete non-streaming response from the Responses API\n\ncompleted_at\n\ninteger | null required\n\ncreated_at\n\nError of a failed response; `metadata` carries OpenRouter-specific details.\n\n`{ \"code\": \"server_error\", \"message\": \"Alignment plugin: the reply could not be evaluated: evaluator_error\", \"metadata\": { \"alignment\": { \"calls\": [ { \"call\": 1, \"outcome\": \"unavailable\", \"reason\": \"evaluator_error\" } ] } }}`\n\nfrequency_penalty\n\nnumber | null required\n\nincomplete_details\n\nobject | null required"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/client-sdks/typescript/sdks/responses/README","title":"Responses - OpenRouter | Documentation","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"| --- | --- |\n| `request` | operations.CreateResponsesRequest | ✔️ | The request object to use for the request. |\n| ` ... | Used to set various options for making HTTP requests. |\n| ` ... extra headers for examples. All `Request` options, except"}],"logprobs":[]}]}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"max_output_tokens":null,"temperature":1,"top_p":1,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0,"top_logprobs":0,"max_tool_calls":null,"metadata":{},"background":false,"previous_response_id":null,"service_tier":"auto","truncation":"disabled","store":false,"instructions":null,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"}},"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7963,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1670,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":499},"total_tokens":9633,"cost":0.016416095,"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.002416095,"upstream_inference_input_cost":0.001313895,"upstream_inference_output_cost":0.0011022},"server_tool_use_details":{"web_search_requests":2,"tool_calls_requested":2,"tool_calls_executed":2}}},"sequence_number":568}

